# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_o.tlk - bulk Surface push O: opinions asked and given, with
# the answer's reply act (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool
# act, no guard change. Rule names end in _uo. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.ask_opinion.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I think it's great. I'd say so without hesitation." guard: topic
  "My honest view? It's a good one, and I like it a lot." guard: topic
  "I'm a fan, if I'm honest. Good call on that." guard: topic
  "I'd vote yes on it. It's a good kind of thing." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Honest view? Not great, and I'd change it if I could." guard: topic
  "I'd skip it. It's a bit much for my taste, sorry." guard: topic
  "My view is not kind, but I'd rather be honest than nice." guard: !topic
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo3 act: answer
  "I think it's okay. Could be better, could be worse." guard: topic
  "Mixed, honestly. It has its moments, and some dull ones." guard: topic
  "I'd say it's fine. Not the best, not the worst either." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo4 act: joke
  "My opinion? It's a strong one, and it's mostly about snacks." guard: topic
  "I'd give it a three out of ten, and a hug for effort." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo5 act: change_topic
  "I'd rather not have an opinion on that. Let's chat about something else." guard: topic
  "Oof, that one's hard. Can we move on to something lighter?" guard: topic
@rule core.ask_opinion.uo6 act: dismiss
  "No opinion, really. Next subject, please." guard: !topic
@rule core.opine_pos.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I agree, it's a good one, and it's a joy to see." guard: topic
  "Yes, and the best part is how easy it is to like." guard: topic
  "Exactly, and I'd add that it's a bit of a treat too." guard: topic
@rule core.opine_neg.uo1 act: opine_neg
  "I don't like it either, and I'd add a few more complaints." guard: topic
  "Right, and the rest of it is worse, if I'm honest." guard: topic
@rule core.opine_pos.uo2 act: laugh
  "Ha, you really like it, don't you? It's all over your face." guard: topic
  "Hee, that's a big thumbs up. I'm impressed." guard: topic
@rule core.opine_neg.uo2 act: sympathize
  "Oh, I'm sorry. That sounds like a rough one to deal with." guard: topic
  "I know that feeling. It's not fun when things go sideways." guard: topic
@rule core.tell.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "That's a nice way to see it. I like that about you."
  "Good for you, that sounds like a fine plan, honestly."
@rule core.tell.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Hm, that's not my favorite story, but I can see why."
  "Ugh, that's the kind of thing I'd rather not hear."
@rule core.tell.uo3 act: continue
  "And then? Don't leave me hanging, go on."
  "Right, and after that? I'm hooked, honestly."
@rule core.answer.uo1 act: agree
  "That's a good answer. I'd agree with you there, mostly."
  "Nice answer. I like the way you put it."
@rule core.answer.uo2 act: disagree
  "Hm, that's a bit of a downer. Still, I see the point."
@rule core.ask_about.uo1 act: opine_pos
  "I really like that one. You picked a good topic." guard: topic
  "That's a favorite of mine. I could talk about it all day." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_about.uo2 act: opine_neg
  "Not my favorite, sorry. It's a bit of a sore spot for me." guard: topic
  "I'd rather skip that one, if you don't mind too much." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_about.uo3 act: answer
  "It's all right. Not one I think about much, to be honest." guard: topic
  "I'd say it's fine. It does what it's meant to, I suppose." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_about.uo4 act: change_topic
  "Hm, that's a big question. Can we talk about something lighter?" guard: topic
  "Let's move on, I'm not sure I've got a good answer for that." guard: topic
@rule core.ask_about.uo5 act: tell
  "Ah, that's a good one. Let me tell you what I remember." guard: topic
  "Funny you ask. I've got a story about that, actually." guard: topic
